{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1030,1060p;1220,1260p;1345,1385p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1030\t(defn- pending-eval\n  1031\t  \"Answer a round whose require did not complete: the parked VM, its\n  1032\t   round-start base, and the pending links are the shell's\n  1033\t   `:pending-run`, and the prompt returns.  Nothing is wedged: another\n  1034\t   line re-checks the link, the host may step one itself with\n  1035\t   `recheck-pending`, the link policy is consulted as the run parks, and\n  1036\t   `(reset)` or `(vm ...)` drops it with the session.\"\n  1037\t  [state state' vm' pending]\n  1038\t  (let [[state'' text] (drain-output state')]\n  1039\t    (consult-link-policy\n  1040\t      (assoc state''\n  1041\t             :vm vm'\n  1042\t             :pending-run {:vm vm'\n  1043\t                           :base (:vm state)\n  1044\t                           :links pending\n  1045\t                           :checks 0})\n  1046\t      text\n  1047\t      (pending-text pending))))\n  1048\t\n  1049\t\n  1050\t(defn- wedged-program\n  1051\t  [state]\n  1052\t  (ex-info\n  1053\t    \"Program stream did not form a complete, runnable Yin VM program.\n  1054\tHint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n  1055\t    {:vm-type (:vm-type state)}))\n  1056\t\n  1057\t\n  1058\t(defn- run-evaluation\n  1059\t  \"The evaluator half of a round whose expander forwarded a program: run\n  1060\t   it, then either finalize the value, drive its require to a conclusion,\n  1220\t\n  1221\t(declare repl-state)\n  1222\t\n  1223\t\n  1224\t(defn handle-command\n  1225\t  \"Answer one shell command.  Unsupported arguments are answered as text, not\n  1226\t   thrown, so a mistyped command cannot end a step.\"\n  1227\t  [state form]\n  1228\t  (let [[command & args] form]\n  1229\t    (case command\n  1230\t      vm (let [vm-type (first args)]\n  1231\t           (if (contains? vm-constructors vm-type)\n  1232\t             [(rebuild-session state vm-type)\n  1233\t              (str \"Switched to \" (get vm-labels vm-type) \" (store cleared)\")]\n  1234\t             [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL VM type \" (pr-str vm-type)\n  1235\t                         \"; supported: \"\n  1236\t                         (pr-str (vec (keys vm-constructors))))]))\n  1237\t      lang (let [lang (first args)]\n  1238\t             (if (contains? lang-labels lang)\n  1239\t               [(assoc state :lang lang)\n  1240\t                (str \"Switched to \" (get lang-labels lang))]\n  1241\t               [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL language \" (pr-str lang)\n  1242\t                           \"; supported: \" (pr-str (vec (keys lang-labels))))]))\n  1243\t      compile [state (render-compile-output\n  1244\t                       state\n  1245\t                       (compile-command-ast state (first args)))]\n  1246\t      reset [(rebuild-session state (:vm-type state))\n  1247\t             (str (get vm-labels (:vm-type state)) \" reset\")]\n  1248\t      abandon (abandon-pending state)\n  1249\t      help [state help-text]\n  1250\t      repl-state [state (format-value (repl-state state))]\n  1251\t      quit [(assoc state :running? false) \"Bye\"]\n  1252\t      telemetry [state telemetry-text]\n  1253\t      [state (str \"Error: Unknown Yin REPL command \" (pr-str command))])))\n  1254\t\n  1255\t\n  1256\t(defn- eval-parsed*\n  1257\t  \"The parse dispatch of one line, against a shell with no require to\n  1258\t   re-check.\"\n  1259\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n  1260\t  (try\n  1345\t\n  1346\t\n  1347\t(defn recheck-pending\n  1348\t  \"One re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` without an input line --\n  1349\t   the step an unattended host drives at its own cadence\n  1350\t   (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 4): serve the interpreter, run the\n  1351\t   parked VM, and consult the link policy when the run is still\n  1352\t   pending.  A re-check that completes the run folds the retained lines\n  1353\t   exactly as a typed line's completion does.  Returns `[state text]`,\n  1354\t   `text` nil when nothing is pending.  It reads no clock and takes no\n  1355\t   callback; the host decides when to call it.\"\n  1356\t  [state]\n  1357\t  (if (:pending-run state)\n  1358\t    (recheck-pending* state nil)\n  1359\t    [state nil]))\n  1360\t\n  1361\t\n  1362\t(defn- resume-pending\n  1363\t  \"One bounded re-check of the shell's `:pending-run` behind a typed\n  1364\t   line: while the run stays pending the line is retained -- the parked\n  1365\t   VM owns the store a new evaluation would fork -- and it evaluates,\n  1366\t   in typing order and exactly once, when the link completes.\"\n  1367\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n  1368\t  (recheck-pending* state {:trimmed trimmed, :parsed parsed}))\n  1369\t\n  1370\t\n  1371\t(defn- command-line?\n  1372\t  [parsed]\n  1373\t  (let [forms (:forms parsed)\n  1374\t        form (when (= 1 (count forms)) (first forms))]\n  1375\t    (and form (command-form? form))))\n  1376\t\n  1377\t\n  1378\t(defn- eval-parsed\n  1379\t  [state trimmed parsed]\n  1380\t  (if (and (:pending-run state) (not (command-line? parsed)))\n  1381\t    ;; A require is still pending: re-check it first.  While it stays\n  1382\t    ;; pending the line is retained -- the parked VM owns the store a new\n  1383\t    ;; evaluation would fork -- and it evaluates, in typing order and\n  1384\t    ;; exactly once, when the link completes.\n  1385\t    (resume-pending state trimmed parsed)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
